<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Analysts see fall in Danish Feb reserves.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Analysts see fall in Danish Feb reserves.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five Danish economists polled by Reuters in a survey issued on Monday foresaw Denmark's February foreign reserves falling on average to 95.4 billion crowns from January's 96.3 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The estimates ranged from a low 93.3 billion crowns to a high 96.3 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The Danish Central Bank is to issue its foreign reserves data for February on Tuesday March 4 at 1500 gmt.</p>
<p>--Stig Pedersen, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
